        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Tetranuclear Dy cubane with two air-stable BPyTz radical ligands. χT at 300 K is 53.71 cm3 K mol−1 (1000 Oe). Weak low-T upturn indicates antiferromagnetic Dy–radical coupling, weaker than in 2. Zero-field ac susceptibility shows only tails of χ″ peaks; slow relaxation is present but Ueff could not be fully extracted. Electrostatic analysis gives mJ = ±15/2 ground doublets with anisotropy-axis deviations of 21.8° (toward TFA) and 17.8° (toward tetrazine).",
