        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Isostructural Dy4 cubane with DBM instead of acac, giving stronger Dy–BPyTz•− antiferromagnetic coupling (χT upturn more pronounced; S-shaped M vs H). Zero-field SMM: frequency- and temperature-dependent χ″ fitted to a generalized Debye model (1.8–5.5 K). Combined Orbach/Raman/QTM fit: Ueff/kB = 31.44(3) K, τ0 = 5.51(9)×10−9 s, C = 0.55(5) s−1 K−n, n = 8.7(8), τQTM = 8.44(8)×10−3 s; Arrhenius approximation 36.53(5) K. Anisotropy axes closer to TFA (5.19°) and tetrazine (12.2°) than in 1.",
